'''2001 Massachusetts State Championship''' was a Star Wars CCG state championship held in Massachusetts in 2001.<ref name="dt-15588">[http://www.decktech.net/starwarsccg/deck/15588 Ten Numb Superstar], DeckTech (Mike "Deck" Gemme, 26 April 2001). Preservation copies: [https://www.stephenskilton.com/decktech_archives/15588/ Stephen Skilton]; [https://stevetotheizz0.github.io/decktech_archives/15588/ GitHub Pages].</ref>

* '''Dates:''' 2001 (before 26 April)
* '''Site:''' Massachusetts
* '''Format:''' [[Premiere - Reflections II]]
* '''Winner:''' —

The event is known from players' DeckTech posts; they give no exact date. It was played before the [[Tatooine (expansion)|Tatooine]] expansion was released on 30 May 2001.

== Results ==

Results below come from players' own DeckTech deck posts. Each row cites the post that gives it. A Dark or Light cell shows — until the deck page is linked.

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Finish !! Player !! Dark !! Light
|-
| 3rd || [[Justin Desai]]<ref name="dt-15554">[http://www.decktech.net/starwarsccg/deck/15554 H2O's mass states deck--3rd place], DeckTech (Justin "H2O" Desai, 24 April 2001). Preservation copies: [https://www.stephenskilton.com/decktech_archives/15554/ Stephen Skilton]; [https://stevetotheizz0.github.io/decktech_archives/15554/ GitHub Pages].</ref> || — || [[2001 Massachusetts State Championship Justin Desai H2O's mass states deck--3rd place|Watch Your Step]]
|-
| Two losses || [[Mike Gemme]]<ref name="dt-15588" /> || — || [[2001 Massachusetts State Championship Mike Gemme Ten Numb Superstar|Quiet Mining Colony]]
|}

Gemme, posting with his playtest partner Steebo, played a version of [[Alex Klammrodt]]'s Quiet Mining Colony deck. It lost only to [[Hayes Hunter]]'s deck, played by Steebo Baroni, and to a Dark sacrifice deck.<ref name="dt-15588" /> Desai finished 3rd with a Light Watch Your Step deck; his only loss was to Hayes Hunter's Abyssin deck.<ref name="dt-15554" /> For the previous year's event see [[2000 Massachusetts State Championship]].

